                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_401">Northampton,
                        Northamptonshire. Cluniac priory of St Andrew. </orgName><p>?fos.
                        1--302</p><p>'Stephanus Cantuariensis super Iob in xxxiii libris' (top of
                        fo. [1]r, xiv c. Below, in xv c. hand '.E.W.')</p><p>'Isti viii quaterni
                        dantur Priori et Conuentui sancti Andr' Norht' ad orandum pro anima domini
                        Willelmi Forde remansuri ibidem imperpetuum' (foot of fo. [302]v (end of
                        Innoc. IV), xiv c.)</p><p>Front flyleaves made up of list of rents, and
                        contain a memorandum on a grant by the prior of St Andrew's
                        Northampton.</p><p>Th modern foliation (and Coxe's catalogue references) is
                        faulty. The fragment of Langton on Maccabees begins on fo. 303, not 203, and
                        the following items on fos. 338 etc.</p><p>For fos. 338--339v, 340--349v,
                        356--367 see S. Kuttner, Repertorium der Kanonistik: Prodromus corporis
                        glossarum I. (Studi e Testi 71), 249, 295, 199.</p><p>The hand which writes
                        the title on fo. 1r is apparently that which write the title in Bodl. Auct.
                        D.1.8, fo. iiv, a St Andrew's book: further, the mark .E.3. in Auct. D.1.8,
                        fo. 1r bears some resemblance to the mark '.E.W.'</p><p>ff. 219--302 are 7
                        quires. ?a quire missing before f. 219</p><q type="pressmark"
                     >.E.W.</q></provenance>
